Notes.Body:
Take the "Render a source template with variables" example above, whose `nginx.conf.jinja` source contains:

```nginx
worker_processes {{ worker_count }};
error_log /var/log/nginx/error.log {{ log_level }};
```

With `defaults: {worker_count: 4}` and `context: {worker_count: 8}`, it renders `worker_processes` as 8 — `context` overrides the default of 4 — while `facts` and `settings` stay available under their own namespaces for any other expressions.
